Optional, not required for rc4
==============================

sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-popup.dtsi only describes the front sensor on cci1
master 1 when CAMERA_WIDE is selected, because the rc3 rear description
instantiates `cci1` (0xac4b000) only inside `#ifdef CAMERA_WIDE` and dtc rejects
an endpoint that points at a compiled-out node.

That is fine for the full DTB and for the rear-wide isolate.  Apply this
one-line widening only if you later want a popup-only isolate DTB
(-DCAMERA_ISOLATE -DCAMERA_POPUP_FRONT without CAMERA_WIDE).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-rear.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-rear.dtsi
@@ -388,7 +388,7 @@
-#ifdef CAMERA_WIDE
+#if defined(CAMERA_WIDE) || defined(CAMERA_POPUP_FRONT)
 	cci1: cci@ac4b000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,sm8150-cci", "qcom,sdm845-cci";
 		#address-cells = <1>;

Effect: the rear-wide isolate DTB gains nothing (CAMERA_WIDE already true); the
new combination CAMERA_ISOLATE + CAMERA_POPUP_FRONT gets cci1 so the sensor node
can be compiled.  Nothing here enables the motor.
